<section>
  <h2>Can I hire a guard for only a few days?</h2>
  <p>Yes. {{ site.name }} accepts requests for 1, 2, 3, 4 or a few days for weddings, puja pandals, events and home guarding during travel. A request becomes a booking after the office confirms staffing, duties, shift times and the written quote. A booking for one day does not mean one person works continuously for 24 hours.</p>
</section>
<section>
  <h2>Which duty should I request?</h2>
  <dl class="faq">
    <div class="faq-item"><dt>Wedding entrance guard or darwan</dt><dd>Describe entrance checks, guest directions, vehicle access and the ceremony schedule. Tell the office how many entrances are open and who will provide the guest list. Identify the venue organiser who can resolve entry questions.</dd></div>
    <div class="faq-item"><dt>Bouncers for a wedding or reception</dt><dd>Discuss crowd control, access restrictions and how staff should report incidents to the organiser. Ask the office to confirm the team's responsibilities and supervision. Bouncers do not replace police or emergency services.</dd></div>
    <div class="faq-item"><dt>Puja pandal guards</dt><dd>Separate visitor-entry and queue duties during opening hours from overnight property guarding. Share the committee contact, public entrances, delivery access and the items that need a handover record.</dd></div>
    <div class="faq-item"><dt>Home guards while your family travels</dt><dd>Specify gate or perimeter duties, visiting workers and authorised access. Agree on a reporting contact, key handover if needed, and arrival and departure times. Avoid posting travel dates, access codes or home security details publicly; discuss sensitive arrangements directly with the office.</dd></div>
  </dl>
</section>
<section>
  <h2>What information does the office need for a quote?</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Exact venue or property address and Google Maps pin.</li>
    <li>Start and end dates, plus daily duty start and finish times.</li>
    <li>Type of guard duty, entrances or posts to cover, and expected guest numbers for events.</li>
    <li>Day shifts, night shifts or continuous cover. Discuss separate shifts, relief and handovers for continuous cover.</li>
    <li>On-site contact and any access or reporting requirements.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Short-term quotes depend on the location, number of posts, duty hours, duration, responsibilities and staffing available. Monthly guard rates shown elsewhere on this site are not one-day event rates. Ask for a written quote showing the agreed scope, charges, payment terms and cancellation terms.</p>
</section>
<section>
  <h2>What should I verify before confirming?</h2>
  <p>Check the agency's legal identity and request the relevant current licence and compliance documents for your assignment. Our legal name is {{ site.legalName }}, CIN {{ site.registrations.cin }}. See our <a href="/pages/compliance/">compliance information and document-request process</a>.</p>
  <p>Confirm the number of posts and staff per shift, uniform requirements, named supervisor or reporting contact, replacement arrangements, and incident-reporting procedure. Keep those details with your accepted quote. Venue map references on our service pages help with planning; they do not indicate that a venue is our client or partner.</p>
</section>

